# closure_owned_capture_across_await - a closure in an async function holds what it captures across a suspend: a `move` closure's owned capture (a String, a value with a destructor) reads the same after each `await`, and is released once, when the future ends; a value carried across one suspend can be moved into a closure made after it; a closure that borrows, made between suspends, leaves the variable to the frame.
